# No em dashes in app copy

Never use em dashes (—) or en dashes (–) in any user-visible text: UI strings, placeholders, chat/assistant messages, notifications, error messages, share texts and seeded/demo content. This also applies to AI-generated copy; prompts for models that produce user-visible text must instruct them to avoid em dashes.

Rewrite with a comma, a period, a colon or the word itself:

```text
❌ Tell me what you want to host—in your own words.
✅ Tell me what you want to host, in your own words.

❌ Sounds great — I noted the details.
✅ Sounds great! I noted the details.
```

A plain hyphen between words ("invite-only", "plus-ones") is fine. Code comments are not affected by this rule.
